type ListAuthAttempts200JSONResponse struct {
	// BlindSpots **Required, and required to be non-empty in any honest
	// implementation.** The ways of failing to get online that
	// leave no row here at all. An empty result set for a MAC
	// means *we have no record*, and a console that renders that
	// as *nothing went wrong* is the exact failure this document
	// exists to prevent — so the reasons travel with the result
	// rather than living in the client's copy, where a future
	// backend could not correct them.
	BlindSpots []AuthBlindSpot `json:"blindSpots"`
	Items      []AuthAttempt   `json:"items"`

	// MacCoverage Whether this deployment records the client MAC on authentication attempts at
	// all — that is, whether the generated `post-auth` query populates
	// `CallingStationId`.
	//
	// **Three-valued, and required, for the reason `NasProbe` is.** A console that
	// searches by MAC and finds nothing has learned one of two completely different
	// things: *this guest never tried*, or *we do not write that column*. Collapsing
	// them into an empty list is how an operator concludes a guest is lying.
	// `unknown` is a deployment whose data plane has not been inspected — not a
	// deployment that records nothing.
	//
	// **It covers `source: radius` and nothing else.** The other two streams are
	// Foyer's own and always carry the MAC the driver verified, so a `not-recorded`
	// deployment still has the address on every `portal` and `driver` row in the
	// same list. A console that renders this as one banner over a mixed page is
	// stating something true about part of it; the wording has to carry that
	// qualifier, and the per-row case inside a `recorded` deployment already has its
	// own copy. See `listAuthAttempts`.
	MacCoverage MacCoverage `json:"macCoverage"`

	// NextCursor Null when there is no further page. There is deliberately no total —
	// see `listSessions`.
	NextCursor *string `json:"nextCursor"`
}

